  "id": "attention-deficit-hyperactivity-disorder",
  "term": "attention-deficit/hyperactivity disorder",
  "definition": "Attention-deficit/hyperactivity disorder is a diagnosis marked by a persistent pattern of inattention and/or hyperactive-impulsive behavior that does not fit the person’s developmental level and significantly disrupts functioning in at least two settings, such as home and school. Recognized presentations include combined, inattentive/distractible, and hyperactive/impulsive types.",
